{#
  view/j-user/users/create-role.phtml — a new role.

  The smallest form on the surface: a name, a parent, and whether new accounts get it
  automatically. `parentId`'s options are the role table itself, so they are data and are
  rendered untranslated — the `false` argument, i.e.
  `$this->formSelect()->setTranslatorEnabled(false)` in the .phtml.

  `isDefault` deserves a second look before anyone ticks it: a default role is granted to
  every account at registration, which is what makes `lib_user`, `pub_user`, `sch_user` and
  `bib_user` mean "signed in" rather than "privileged", and therefore what makes every route
  guard naming one of them toothless. Nothing here
  warns about that, and reproducing the page faithfully means not adding a warning in the
  same change that moves it.

  The `<h1>` translates since 2026-08-21 — see the note in user-edit.html.twig for what it
  used to do and why.

  **These two pages close their `<form>` and the .phtml did not.** Neither `create.phtml`
  nor `create-role.phtml` calls `closeTag()` — they end at `formSubmit()` — so laminas
  serves an unclosed `<form>` that a browser has to close for it at `</body>`, taking the
  footer into the form on the way. Emitting `</form>` is the only other deliberate
  difference in this batch besides the delete page's missing name: every field and the
  submit button are already above it, nothing after it is an input, and an unclosed form
  element is invalid HTML rather than a style choice.
#}
{% extends juser_layout %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate(page_title) }}</h1>

{{ form_open(form, '') }}
{{ form_row(form.get('name')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('parentId'), false) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('isDefault')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('security')) }}
{{ form_submit(form.get('submit')) }}
{{ form_close() }}
{% endblock %}
